{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 48, :comments ["<b>And he shall make a pesaḥ.</b> Who comes to make a pesaḥ." "<b>And he shall be as a native of the land.</b> Since he heard the account of the miracles of HaKadosh Barukh Hu and came to take refuge under His wings, even though his fathers were not present at that miracle. If he converted between the two pesaḥim, I might think he should make the second pesaḥ — Scripture says, <b>and he shall be as a native of the land</b>: just as a native, if he was exempt from the first, does not make the second, so too a convert." "<b>And every uncircumcised person shall not eat of it.</b> Because it is repulsive, as stated in the chapter 'One who was tamei.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:32.455383563Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}